  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0137_e9d6ddfb9426.png\" style=\"width: 141px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Assume a complete sphere, then&nbsp;flux&nbsp;due to a charge placed at the center of sphere is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Flux through hemisphere surface is equal to flux passing through flat surface&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0137_436f20ea99e6.png\" style=\"width: 147px; height: 110px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
